OrionLayer open fix 115 — the Turn Summary's messages carry their engine type
==============================================================================

Work order 384. orion2re on the fork's branch `orionlayer` (v2.0.0), on top
of open fix 111, amended; commit 5a09e0ba. Not on `orionlayer-local`. In
src/ext/ext_api.cpp only, under ORION2RE_EXT.

The Turn Summary (TPOP kind 2) sent each message as its text, its field and
its list page. HD ranks the summary by what a message IS (a colony's
building scrapped, a product finished, a ship lost ...); the words are the
player's language and not a key. The engine knows the type: every message
has msg_type (MSG_TYPE_*), and a colony message its subtype
(MSG_COLONY_SUBTYPE_*), its planet and a union of numbers.

The change. The TPOP block of kind 2 is block version 2; every other kind
stays version 1. Per message, after its field count (uint8 n_fields):
uint8 MSG_TYPE_*, uint8 MSG_COLONY_SUBTYPE_* (255 when the message is not a
colony message), int16 the colony message's planet (-1 otherwise), int16 a
and int16 b: for BUILDING_SCRAPPED the building's id and its refund, for
PRODUCTION_COMPLETED the product's id and 0, else 0 and 0.

The cost: a few bytes per message, once per snapshot while the popup is
up. Nothing else is sent or changed.

Live: proved by work order 384 (scratch-clone syntax check with a
misspelt-constant control, then a live run). Revert: git revert 5a09e0ba.

